WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.617 --> 00:00:05.694
There is a second kind of error, though.

2
00:00:05.694 --> 00:00:11.847
A phase flip leaves every bit where it was, and only changes the sign between them.

3
00:00:11.847 --> 00:00:14.924
Our parity checks cannot see it at all.

4
00:00:15.617 --> 00:00:22.155
The fix is to also check in a rotated basis, where phase flips look like bit flips.

5
00:00:22.155 --> 00:00:27.540
Do both, everywhere, on a two dimensional grid, and you get the surface code.

6
00:00:28.217 --> 00:00:30.140
White circles are data qubits.

7
00:00:30.140 --> 00:00:32.447
Teal squares check for bit flips.

8
00:00:32.447 --> 00:00:34.755
Violet squares check for phase flips.

9
00:00:34.755 --> 00:00:38.601
Each check touches four neighbors, or two along the edge.

10
00:00:39.283 --> 00:00:43.129
Flip one qubit and the checks beside it light up.

11
00:00:43.129 --> 00:00:47.360
Flip a whole chain, and only its two ends light up.

12
00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:49.668
Everything in between cancels in pairs.

13
00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:52.273
And that is the catch.

14
00:00:52.273 --> 00:00:57.273
A chain from one edge to the other lights up nothing at all,

15
00:00:57.273 --> 00:00:59.581
yet it flips the stored information.

16
00:00:59.581 --> 00:01:04.196
The shortest such chain has length d, the distance of the code.
